hadiths[178]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17423","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarani Yahya ibn Said from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Abu Said from Abdullah ibn Malik that the sister of Uqbah ibn Amir vowed to perform Hajj walking, so Uqbah asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, so he said Order her to ride. So he thought he had not understood him, then when those with him were gone he returned and asked him, so he said Order her to ride, for Allah, mighty and majestic, is in no need of your sister tormenting herself."
"17424","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarani Yunus from al-Hasan from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said There is no liability after four."
"17425","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salamah from Ibn Ishaq from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in Maghrib wearing a silk farruj, which is the qaba, then when he finished his prayer he pulled it off with a violent pull and said This does not befit the God-fearing."
"17426","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salamah from Ibn Ishaq from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah al-Tujibi from Uqbah ibn Amir who said I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say A tax collector will not enter Paradise, meaning the ushar."
"17427","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Ibn Ishaq who said haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Juhani who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said I shall ride tomorrow to the Jews, so do not greet them first, and if they greet you say Wa alaykum."
"17428","Abdullah said My father said Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar and Ibn Lahiah differed with him, saying from Abu Basrah. Haddathana Abu Asim from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, Abu Basrah said, meaning in the hadith of Ibn Abi Adi, from Ibn Ishaq."
"17429","Haddathana al-Walid ibn Muslim who said haddathana Ibn Jabir from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman from Uqbah ibn Amir who said While I was leading the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a mountain pass among those passes, he said to me O Uqbah, will you not ride. He said So I deemed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, too exalted for me to ride his mount. Then he said O Uqayb, will you not ride. He said So I feared it would be disobedience. He said So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, alighted and I rode a while, then he rode. Then he said O Uqayb, shall I not teach you two surahs among the best two surahs the people recite. He said I said Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said So he taught me Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. Then the prayer was established and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went forward and recited them, then passed by me. He said How do you see, O Uqayb, recite them whenever you sleep and whenever you rise. Abu Abd al-Rahman said He is Uqbah ibn Amir ibn Abis, and Ibn Abs said al-Juhani."
"17430","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, haddathana Shayban from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim that Abu Abd al-Rahman told him that Ibn Abis al-Juhani told him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him O Ibn Abis, shall I not tell you of the best by which seekers of refuge seek refuge. He said I said Yes. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, these two surahs."
"17431","Haddathana Hasan who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah who said haddathana Abu Ushshanah that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir say from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said Whoever loses three from his loins and counts them for Allah, mighty and majestic, and Abu Ushshanah once said in the path of Allah and did not say it another time, Paradise becomes due for him."
"17432","Haddathana Hafs ibn Ghiyath from Ismail from Qays from Uqbah ibn Amir who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Two surahs were revealed to me, so seek refuge by them, for refuge was never sought with the like of them, meaning the Muawwidhatayn."
"17433","Haddathana Ismail ibn Ibrahim, haddathana Hisham from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir who said haddathana Abu Sallam from Abdullah al-Azraq from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, admits three by a single arrow into Paradise, its maker who seeks good in his making, and the one who supplies it, and the one who shoots it. And he said Shoot and ride, and shooting is dearer to me than riding. And everything by which a man amuses himself is false except a man shooting with his bow and training his horse and playing with his wife, for they are from the truth. And whoever forgets shooting after being taught it has disbelieved in what he was taught."
"17434","Haddathana Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash who said haddathani Muhammad the freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said haddathani Kab ibn Alqamah from Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn Abdullah from Uqbah ibn Amir who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath."
"17435","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar who said haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani from Uqbah ibn Amir who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said The most deserving conditions to be fulfilled are those by which you make private parts lawful."
"17436","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Ismail who said haddathani Qays from Uqbah ibn Amir from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said Verses were revealed to me the like of which were never seen, Say I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind to the end of the surah, and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak to the end of the surah."
"17437","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Hisham al-Dastuwai who said haddathana Yahya from Bahjah ibn Abdullah from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided sacrifices among his companions, and Uqbah ibn Amir received a jadhaah, so he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about it, so he said Sacrifice it."
"17438","Haddathana al-Hakam ibn Nafi who said haddathana Ibn Ayyash from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah al-Aslami from Abu Ali al-Hamdani who said I went out on a journey and with us was Uqbah ibn Amir. He said So we said to him May Allah have mercy on you, you are among the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so lead us. So he said No, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say Whoever leads the people, if he gets the time right and completes the prayer, then for him and for them, and whoever falls short of that in anything, then upon him and not upon them."
"17439","Haddathana Waki who said haddathana Sufyan from Yahya ibn Said from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Abu Said al-Ruayni from Abdullah ibn Malik al-Yahsabi from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani that his sister vowed to walk barefoot uncovered, so he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said Allah does nothing with the hardship of your sister, order her to cover and to ride and to fast three days."
"17440","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq who said akhbarana Abdullah meaning Ibn al-Mubarak who said akhbarana Ibn Lahiah who said haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib who said haddathana Abu al-Khayr that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir say the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said The parable of one who does evil deeds then does good deeds is like a man with a tight coat of mail that choked him, then he did a good deed and a ring loosened, then he did another good deed and another ring loosened, until he comes out to open ground."
"17441","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, haddathana Abdullah meaning Ibn al-Mubarak who said haddathana Harmalah ibn Imran who said haddathani Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Mulayl al-Sulayhi, and they are toward Qudaah, who said haddathani my father who said I was with Uqbah ibn Amir sitting near the minbar on Friday, then Muhammad ibn Abi Hudhayfah came and mounted the minbar and addressed the people, then recited to them a surah of the Quran, and he was among the most reciting of people. He said So Uqbah ibn Amir said Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say Men will recite the Quran not passing their throats, they pass out of religion as the arrow passes out of the game."
"17442","Haddathana Attab ibn Ziyad who said haddathana Abdullah who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah, akhbarani Yazid ibn Amr al-Maafiri from one who heard Uqbah ibn Amir say The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me as a collector, so I asked his permission to eat from the charity, so he permitted us."
"17443","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan who said haddathana Rishdin meaning Ibn Sad who said haddathani Amr meaning Ibn al-Harith from Abu Ushshanah that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir report from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to forbid the people of ornament and silk and say If you love the ornament of Paradise and its silk, do not wear them in this world."
"17444","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan who said haddathana Rishdin meaning Ibn Sad, Abu al-Hajjaj al-Mahri, from Harmalah ibn Imran al-Tujibi from Uqbah ibn Muslim from Uqbah ibn Amir from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said If you see Allah giving the servant from this world for his sins what he loves, it is only gradual leading on. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited When they forgot what they were reminded of, We opened upon them the doors of everything until when they rejoiced in what they were given, We seized them suddenly, then they were in despair."
"17445","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Said who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah from Abu Ushshanah from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Your Lord marvels at a shepherd of sheep on a mountain crag calling the adhan for prayer and establishing it."
"17446","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Said who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah from al-Harith ibn Yazid from Ali ibn Rabah from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said These lineages of yours are not reproach upon anyone, you are only the children of Adam, like an unfilled sa measure, no one has merit except by religion or righteous deed, enough for a man to be obscene, foul-mouthed, miserly, cowardly."
"17447","Haddathana Abu al-Ala al-Hasan ibn Sawwar who said haddathana Layth from Muawiyah from Abu Uthman from Jubayr ibn Nufayr and Rabiah ibn Yazid from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, and Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht from al-Layth ibn Sulaym al-Juhani, all of them narrate from Uqbah ibn Amir who said Uqbah said We used to serve ourselves and take turns herding camels among us, so my turn herding camels befell me, and I brought them in the evening and found the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, standing addressing the people, and I caught from his speech while he said There is none among you who performs ablution and does it well, then stands and prays two rakahs facing them with his heart and face, except Paradise becomes due for him and he is forgiven. He said So I said to him How excellent is this. He said So a speaker before me said That which was before it, O Uqbah, is more excellent. So I looked, and it was Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said So I said What is it, O Abu Hafs. He said He said before you came There is none among you who performs ablution and does it well, then says I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner for Him and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger, except the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, he enters from whichever he wills."
"17448","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Abdullah, akhbarana Said ibn Abi Ayyub who said haddathana Abdullah ibn al-Walid from Abu al-Khayr from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said If healing is in anything, then in the incision of a cupper or a drink of honey or a cauterization hitting pain, and I dislike cauterization and do not love it."
"17449","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq who said haddathana Abdullah, akhbarani Ibn Lahiah who said haddathani Yazid that Abu al-Khayr told him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir narrate from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said No deed of a day but is sealed over it, so when the believer falls ill the angels say O our Lord, such a servant of Yours You have confined, so the Lord, mighty and majestic, says Seal for him like his deed until he recovers or dies."
"17450","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, haddathana Ibn al-Mubarak Abdullah who said haddathana Musa ibn Ali who said I heard my father say I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Learn the Book of Allah and maintain it and chant it, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it escapes more than milch camels from hobbles."
"17451","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah who said haddathana Abu Qabil who said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said I only fear for my nation the Book and milk. He said It was said O Messenger of Allah, what is with the Book. He said Hypocrites learn it then dispute by it with those who believe. So it was said And what is with milk. He said People love milk, so they go out from congregations and leave Fridays."
"17452","Haddathana Hasan who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah who said haddathana Kab ibn Alqamah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah from Abu al-Khayr from Uqbah ibn Amir from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath."
"17453","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan, haddathana Rishdin, haddathana Bakr ibn Amr al-Maafiri, haddathana Shuayb ibn Zurah al-Maafiri, he told him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir say Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says Do not frighten yourselves after your security. They said And what is that, O Messenger of Allah. He said Debt."
"17454","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa who said haddathana Yahya ibn Hamzah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid that Abu Sallam told him who said haddathani Khalid ibn Zayd who said Uqbah used to come to me and say Go out with us to shoot, then I delayed for him one day or was reluctant, so he said I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, admits by a single arrow three into Paradise, its maker who seeks good in it, and the shooter with it, and its supplier, so shoot and ride, and shooting is dearer to me than riding. And there is no amusement except three, a man playing with his wife and training his horse and shooting with his bow. And whoever Allah teaches shooting then leaves it out of dislike, a blessing he has disbelieved."
"17455","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah from Mishrah ibn Haan from Uqbah ibn Amir who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me Recite the Muawwidhatayn, for you will never recite with the like of them."
"17456","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa who said haddathana Attaf from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah from a man of Juhaynah from Uqbah ibn Amir who said I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say There will be leaders over you after me, so if they pray the prayer at its time and complete bowing and prostration, then it is for you and for them, and if they do not pray the prayer at its time nor complete its bowing nor its prostration, then it is for you and upon them."
"17457","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi, haddathana Salamah ibn al-Fadl who said haddathani Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me Recite the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah, for I was given them from under the Throne."
"17458","Haddathana Attab meaning Ibn Ziyad, haddathana Abdullah meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, akhbarana Yahya ibn Ayyub, haddathani Kab ibn Alqamah that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah narrate from Abu al-Khayr who said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath."
"17459","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf from Said from Qatadah who said he mentioned that Qays al-Judhami told him from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Whoever frees a believing slave, it is his ransom from the Fire."
"17460","Haddathana Yaqub who said haddathana my father from Ibn Ishaq who said haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib al-Misri from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah al-Tujibi who said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani say while on the minbar of Egypt I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say It is not lawful for a man to sell over the sale of his brother until he leaves it."
"17461","Haddathana Yaqub who said haddathana my father from Ibn Ishaq who said haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah al-Tujibi from Uqbah ibn Amir who said I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say It is not lawful for a Muslim man to propose over the proposal of his brother until he leaves, nor to sell over the sale of his brother until he leaves."
"17462","Haddathana Yaqub who said haddathana my father from Ibn Ishaq who said haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib al-Misri from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, and Yazan is a clan of Himyar, who said Abu Ayyub Khalid ibn Zayd al-Ansari, the companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us in Egypt as a warrior, and Uqbah ibn Amir ibn Abs al-Juhani, whom Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan had appointed over us, delayed Maghrib, so when he prayed Abu Ayyub al-Ansari stood to him and said to him O Uqbah, thus did you see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray Maghrib, did you not hear him from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say My nation remains in good, or on the fitrah, so long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars intermix. He said So he said Yes. He said So what made you do what you did. He said I was busy. So Abu Ayyub said By Allah, nothing but lest the people think that you saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do this."
"17463","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahiah, haddathana Bakr ibn Sawadah from Abu Said Juthal al-Qitbani from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani from Uqbah ibn Amir that the sister of Uqbah vowed concerning a son of hers to walk to Hajj barefoot without a headcover, so that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said She performs Hajj riding covered, and she shall fast."
"17464","Haddathana Hasan who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah, haddathana Kab ibn Alqamah from Kathir the freedman of Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Whoever conceals a believer is like one who revives a buried girl from her grave."
"17465","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa and Musa ibn Dawud who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah, haddathana Kab ibn Alqamah from a freedman of Uqbah ibn Amir called Kathir who said I met Uqbah ibn Amir and told him that we have neighbors who drink wine. He said Leave them. Then he came to him and said Shall I not call the police against them. So Uqbah said Woe to you, leave them, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say Whoever sees a shame and conceals it is like one who revives a buried girl from her grave."
"17466","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Abdullah ibn Mubarak, akhbarana Harmalah ibn Imran that he heard Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrate that Abu al-Khayr told him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir say I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say Every man is in the shade of his charity until judged between people, or he said decided between people. Yazid said And Abu al-Khayr never missed a day but he gave charity in it with something, even a cake or an onion or such."
"17467","Haddathana Abu al-Mughirah, haddathana Muan ibn Rifaa, haddathani Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah al-Bahili from Uqbah ibn Amir who said I met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and began with him and took his hand. He said So I said O Messenger of Allah, what is the salvation of this matter. He said O Uqbah, guard your tongue and let your house suffice you and weep over your sin. He said Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met me and began with me and took my hand, so he said O Uqbah ibn Amir, shall I not teach you the best three surahs revealed in the Torah and the Gospel and the Psalms and the great Furqan. He said I said Yes, may Allah make me ransom for you. He said So he taught me Say He is Allah One and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. Then he said O Uqbah, do not forget them and do not spend a night until you recite them. He said So I never forgot them since he said Do not forget them, and I never spent a night at all until I recited them. Uqbah said Then I met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and began with him and took his hand, and I said O Messenger of Allah, tell me of excellent deeds. So he said O Uqbah, join whoever cuts you and give whoever deprives you and turn away from whoever wrongs you."
"17468","Haddathana Abu al-Yaman, haddathana Ismail ibn Ayyash from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir from Abu Sallam from Khalid ibn Zayd al-Ansari who said I was with Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, and he was a man who loved shooting, when he went out he took me with him, then he called me one day and I delayed for him, so he said Come, I tell you what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me and told me. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, admits by a single arrow three persons into Paradise, its maker who seeks good in his making, and the shooter with it, and its supplier. And he said Shoot and ride, and shooting is dearer to me than riding. And there is no amusement except three, a man training his horse and playing with his wife and shooting with his bow. And whoever leaves shooting after being taught it out of dislike, it is a blessing he has left."
"17469","Haddathana Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi who said haddathana al-Walid ibn Muslim from Ibn Jabir from Abu Sallam from Khalid ibn Zayd from Uqbah ibn Amir from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said Whoever is taught shooting then leaves it after being taught it, it is a blessing he has disbelieved."
"17470","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Zayd ibn Sallam from Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Azraq who said Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani used to go out and shoot every day, and he would have one follow him as if he was almost bored, so he said Shall I not tell you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said Yes. He said I heard him say Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, admits by a single arrow three persons into Paradise, its owner who seeks good in his making, and the one who prepares it in the path of Allah, and the one who shoots it in the path of Allah. And he said Shoot and ride, and shooting is better than riding. And he said Everything by which the son of Adam amuses himself is false except three, his shooting from his bow and training his horse and playing with his family, for they are from the truth. He said Then Uqbah died leaving sixty odd or seventy odd bows, with each bow a case and arrows, and he bequeathed them in the path of Allah."
"17471","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun who said haddathana Hisham from Yahya from Abu Sallam from Abdullah ibn al-Azraq that Uqbah ibn Amir said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, admits three by a single arrow into Paradise, then he mentioned the hadith."
"17472","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana Ismail meaning Ibn Abi Khalid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aidh a man of the people of Sham who said Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani set out to al-Masjid al-Aqsa to pray in it, so people followed him, so he said What brings you. They said Your companionship to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, we loved to go with you and greet you. He said Alight and pray. So they alighted and he prayed and they prayed with him, so he said when he saluted I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say No servant meets Allah, mighty and majestic, not associating anything with Him, unstained with unlawful blood, except he enters from whichever gates of Paradise he wills."
"17473","Haddathana Abu Said the freedman of Banu Hashim who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah who said haddathana Kab ibn Alqamah who said I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah say We came to Abu al-Khayr, so he said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say A vow is only an oath, its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"17474","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Layth, haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu Imran Aslam from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani that he said I followed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was riding, so I placed my hands on his feet and said Teach me from Surah Yusuf. So he said You will never recite anything more effective with Allah, mighty and majestic, than Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak."
"17475","Haddathana Haywah ibn Shurayh who said haddathana Baqiyyah, haddathana Bahir ibn Sad from Khalid ibn Madan from Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Uqbah ibn Amir that he said Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was gifted a gray mule and rode it, and Uqbah took leading it, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Uqbah Recite. So he said What shall I recite, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Recite Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak. So he repeated it to him until he recited it, and he knew that I did not rejoice greatly in it, so he said Perhaps you deem it light, you never stand praying with anything like it."
"17476","Haddathana Hajjaj and Hashim who said haddathana Layth, haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from Uqbah ibn Amir that he said A silk farruj was gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he wore it then prayed in it, then turned and pulled it off with a violent strong pull as one disliking it, then said This does not befit the God-fearing."
"17477","Haddathana Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, haddathana al-Layth ibn Sad, haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out one day and prayed over the people of Uhud his prayer over the dead, then turned to the minbar and said I am a predecessor for you and a witness over you, and by Allah I look at the Hawd now, and I have been given the keys of the treasures of the earth, or the keys of the earth, by Allah I do not fear for you that you will associate after me, but I fear for you that you will compete in it."
"17478","Haddathana Hajjaj, akhbarana Layth, haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from Uqbah ibn Amir that he said We said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, You send us and we alight with people who do not host us, so what do you see in that. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us If you alight with people and they provide for you what befits a guest, accept, and if they do not, take from them the right of a guest which befits them."
"17479","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Layth ibn Sad, haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him sheep and divided them among his companions as sacrifices, and a young goat remained from them, so he mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said Sacrifice it."
"17480","Haddathana Hajjaj, akhbarana Layth, haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Beware of entering upon women. So a man from the Ansar said O Messenger of Allah, what about the in-law. He said The in-law is death."
"17481","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Abdullah ibn Zahr al-Damri that he heard Abu Said al-Ruayni narrate that Abdullah ibn Malik told him from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, he told him that his sister vowed to walk barefoot uncovered, so Uqbah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Order your sister to ride and to cover and to fast three days."
"17482","Haddathana Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi and Yunus who said haddathana Aban who said haddathana Qatadah from al-Hasan from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said If two guardians marry, she belongs to the first of them, and if one sells to two men, to the first of them. My father said And Yunus said If a man sells a sale to two men."
"17483","Haddathana Zayd ibn al-Hubab, haddathana Muawiyah ibn Salih, haddathana al-Ala ibn al-Harith from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman the freedman of Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan from Uqbah ibn Amir who said I was leading the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said So he said to me Shall I not teach you two surahs never recited with the like of them. I said Yes. So he taught me Say I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak. So he did not see me admire them, then when dawn came he recited them, then said to me How do you see, O Uqbah."
"17484","Haddathana Harun, haddathana Ibn Wahb, akhbarani Jarir ibn Hazim from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah that he said Pray in sheep pens and do not pray in camel resting places or camel sitting places."
"17485","And he said haddathana Ibn Wahb, haddathani Asim ibn Hakim from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Shaybani from his father from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with that."
"17486","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, haddathana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, and haddathana my father from al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, haddathana Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said A silk farruj was gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he wore it and prayed Maghrib in it with the people, then when he saluted from his prayer he pulled it off with a violent pull, then threw it. So we said O Messenger of Allah, you wore it and prayed in it. He said This does not befit the God-fearing."
"17487","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah who said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani say I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say A tax collector will not enter Paradise, meaning the ushar."
"17488","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana Ismail ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Verses were revealed to me I never saw the like of them, the Muawwidhatayn, then he recited them."
"17489","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud who said haddathana Ibn Lahiah from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from Uqbah ibn Amir who said A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said My mother died and I want to give charity for her. He said Did she command you. He said No. He said Then do not do."
"17490","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hisham from Qatadah from Qays al-Judhami from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Whoever frees a Muslim slave, it is his ransom from the Fire."
"17491","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said The warranty of a slave is four nights. Qatadah said And the people of Madinah say three nights."
"17492","Haddathana Abdullah ibn Yazid, haddathana Ibn Lahiah, haddathana Mishrah who said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say Every dead is sealed over his deed except one guarding the frontier in the path of Allah, for the reward of his deed continues for him until he is resurrected."
"17493","Haddathana Qutaybah, he said therein And he is secured from the trial of the grave."
"17494","Haddathana Abdullah ibn Yazid, haddathana Ibn Lahiah who said Abu Abd al-Rahman, I think from Mishrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Best of households are Abu Abdullah and Umm Abdullah and Abdullah."
"17495","Haddathana Abdullah ibn Yazid, haddathana Qabath ibn Razin al-Lakhmi who said I heard Ali ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi say I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani say We were sitting in the mosque reciting the Quran, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered and greeted us, so we returned the greeting to him, then he said Learn the Book of Allah and acquire it. He said And I think he said And chant it, for by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it escapes more than milch camels from hobbles."
"17496","Haddathana Abdullah ibn Yazid, haddathana Ibn Lahiah, and Hashim, haddathana Layth from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say The most deserving conditions to fulfill are those by which you make private parts lawful."
"17497","Haddathana Abdullah ibn Yazid from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, haddathani Zuhrah ibn Mabad from a cousin of his, the brother of his father, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir say the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then raises his gaze to the sky and says I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner for Him and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, he enters from whichever he wills."
"17498","Haddathana Abu Said the freedman of Banu Hashim, haddathana Ibn Lahiah, haddathana Mishrah ibn Haan Abu Musab al-Maafiri who said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say I said O Messenger of Allah, is Surah al-Hajj favored over the rest of the Quran by two prostrations. He said Yes, so whoever does not prostrate them, let him not recite them."
"17499","Haddathana Abu Said, haddathana Ibn Lahiah, haddathana Mishrah who said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said If the Quran were placed in a skin then thrown into the Fire, it would not burn."
"17500","Haddathana Abu Said, haddathana Ibn Lahiah, haddathana Mishrah who said I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me Recite Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, for you never recite with the like of them."
"17501","Abu Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Mishrah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Most of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters."
"17502","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who recites the Quran aloud is like the one who gives charity aloud, and the one who recites the Quran secretly is like the one who gives charity secretly."
"17503","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hammad ibn Khalid was a memorizer, and he used to narrate to us, and he used to memorize; I wrote from him, I and Yahya ibn Main."
"17504","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: I heard a man narrating from Uqbah ibn Amir that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There is no man who dies when he dies while in his heart is the weight of a mustard seed of pride for whom Paradise will be lawful so that he smells its fragrance or sees it. Then a man from Quraysh called Abu Rayhanah said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, indeed I love beauty and desire it, so much that I love it in the strap of my whip and in the lace of my sandal. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is not pride; indeed Allah, Almighty, is Beautiful and loves beauty, but pride is whoever scorns the truth and despises people with his eyes."
"17505","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim: Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Have you not seen verses revealed tonight the like of which has never been seen: the two Muawwidhatayn."
"17506","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah, Almighty, wonders at a youth who has no youthful folly."
"17507","Qutaybah narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The first two litigants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors."
"17508","Qutaybah narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not coerce daughters, for they are the comforting precious ones."
"17509","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami, from one who narrated to him, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed the first bone of man that will speak on the day when mouths are sealed is his thigh from the left leg."
"17510","Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, and Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, that Abu Said, Yazid said, al-Ruayni, informed him that Abdullah ibn Malik informed him that Uqbah ibn Amir informed him that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a sister of his who had vowed to walk barefoot without a headcover, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let her wear a headcover and let her ride and let her fast three days."
"17511","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed the most deserving of conditions to be fulfilled are those by which you made private parts lawful."
"17512","Waki narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ali, from his father, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: There are three hours in which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to forbid us to pray or to bury our dead: when the sun rises shining until it elevates, and when the noon stander stands until the sun declines, and when it inclines toward sunset until it sets."
"17513","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verses were revealed to me the like of which has never been seen, meaning the two Muawwidhatayn."
"17514","Waki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Day of Arafah and the Day of Sacrifice and the days of Tashriq are our Eid, people of Islam, and they are days of eating and drinking."
"17515","Waki narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a jadha, so he said: Sacrifice it, there is no harm in it."
"17516","Waki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aidh, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever meets Allah, Almighty, associating nothing with Him and not stained with unlawful blood, will enter Paradise."
"17517","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: I heard Musa ibn Ali ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi saying: I heard my father saying: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: There are three hours in which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to forbid us to pray in them and to bury our dead in them: when the sun rises shining until it elevates, and at the noon standing until the sun declines, and when it inclines toward sunset until it sets."
"17518","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Musa, meaning Ibn Ali, narrated to us, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed the Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Arafah and the days of Tashriq, they are our Eid, people of Islam, and they are days of eating and drinking."
"17519","Ismail narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The warranty of slaves is three."
"17520","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The warranty of slaves is three days."
"17521","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub informed me that Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed him that Abu al-Khayr narrated to him, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that he said: Indeed my sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah, Almighty, so she ordered me to ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for her, so I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Let her walk and let her ride. He said: And Abu al-Khayr would not part from Uqbah."
"17522","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us that Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed him, then he mentioned the hadith."
"17523","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Juhani who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, two riders appeared, and when he saw them he said: Two Kindis, two Madhhijis, until they came to him, and they were men from Madhhij. He said: Then one of them drew near to him to pledge to him, and when he took his hand he said: O Messenger of Allah, what of one who saw you and believed in you and deemed you truthful and followed you, what is for him? He said: Blessed is he. He said: Then he wiped over his hand and left. Then the other came until he took his hand to pledge to him, he said: O Messenger of Allah, what of one who believed in you and deemed you truthful and followed you and did not see you? He said: Blessed is he, then blessed is he, then blessed is he. He said: Then he wiped over his hand and left."
"17524","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, that Abu Abdullah informed him that Ibn Abis al-Juhani informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O Ibn Abis, shall I not inform you of the best with which those who seek refuge seek refuge? He said: I said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, and: I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak, these two surahs."
"17525","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nuaym ibn Hammar, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah, Almighty, says: O son of Adam, suffice Me at the beginning of the day with four rakahs, I will suffice you with them the rest of your day."
"17526","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Abu Sad al-Ama narrating to Ata, he said: Abu Ayyub traveled to Uqbah ibn Amir, so he came to Maslamah ibn Makhlad, and he came out to him. He said: Guide me, then he came to Uqbah and said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with none remaining who heard it. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever conceals a believer in the world, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection. Then he came to his mount and rode and returned."
"17527","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim, freedman of Muawiyah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I was leading the mount of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in travel, so he said: O Uqbah, shall I not teach you the best two surahs recited? I said: Yes. He said: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak, and say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. Then when he descended he prayed with them the dawn prayer. He said: How do you see, O Uqbah?"
"17528","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Rabiah, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: And Abu Uthman narrated to him, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: Camel-herding was upon us, then my turn came, so I brought them back in the evening, then I found the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, standing addressing the people, so I caught from his speech: There is no Muslim who performs wudu and perfects wudu, then stands and prays two rakahs devoting himself to them with his heart and face, except Paradise becomes due for him. So I said: How excellent this is. Then one speaking before me said: The one before it is more excellent than it. So I looked, and it was Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: Indeed I saw you come just now. He said: There is none among you who performs wudu and completes wudu, then says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and His Messenger, except the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, he enters through whichever he wills."
"17529","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Qabath ibn Razin narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabah, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us while we were studying the Quran. He said: Learn the Quran and acquire it. Qabath said: And I do not know except he said: And chant it melodiously, for it escapes more swiftly than pregnant camels from their hobbles."
"17530","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Nashit al-Khawlani, from Kab ibn Alqamah, from Abu al-Haytham, from Dukhayn, scribe of Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: I said to Uqbah: We have neighbors who drink wine, and I am going to call the police for them so they seize them. So he said: Do not do it, but admonish them and threaten them. He said: So he did, and they did not stop. He said: Then Dukhayn came to him and said: I forbade them and they did not stop, and I am going to call the police for them. So Uqbah said: Woe to you, do not do it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever conceals the private fault of a believer, it is as if he brought to life a buried girl from her grave."
"17531","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Beware of entering upon women. Then a man from the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the in-law? He said: The in-law is death."
"17532","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out one day and prayed over the people of Uhud his prayer over the dead, then went out to the minbar and said: Indeed I am your forerunner, and I am a witness over you, and by Allah I am now looking at my Basin, and I have been given the keys of the treasures of the earth, and by Allah I do not fear for you that you will associate partners after me, but I fear for you that you will compete in it."
"17533","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Azraq, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are two kinds of jealousy, one of which Allah, Almighty, loves and the other Allah hates, and two kinds of pride, one of which Allah, Almighty, loves and the other Allah hates. Jealousy in suspicion Allah, Almighty, loves, and jealousy in other than it Allah hates. And pride when a man gives charity Allah loves, and pride in arrogance Allah hates."
"17534","And he said: Three whose supplication is answered for them: the traveler, and the parent, and the oppressed."
"17535","And he said: Indeed Allah, Almighty, admits by a single arrow three into Paradise: its maker, and the one who supplies it, and the one who shoots it in the way of Allah, Almighty."
"17536","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated to us, from Abu Ali al-Misri who said: We traveled with Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, then prayer came, so we wanted him to lead us. We said: You are from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, yet you will not lead us? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever leads people, if he completes then for him is completion and for them is completion, and if he does not complete then for them is completion and upon him is sin."
"17537","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over the slain of Uhud after eight years like one bidding farewell to the living and the dead, then ascended the minbar and said: Indeed I am your forerunner and I am a witness over you, and your appointment is the Basin, and I am looking at it, and I do not fear for you that you will associate partners, or he said: disbelieve, but the world, that you compete in it."
"17538","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Imran narrated to us, Abu Ushshanah al-Maafiri narrated to me, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever had, and once he said: whoever has three daughters and is patient with them and feeds them and gives them drink and clothes them from his means, they will be for him a veil from the Fire."
"17539","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah informed us, Khalid ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: I heard Mishrah ibn Haan saying: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever hangs a tamimah, may Allah not complete for him, and whoever hangs a wadaah, may Allah not leave him in comfort."
"17540","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr narrated to us that Mishrah ibn Haan informed him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: If there were to be a prophet after me, Umar ibn al-Khattab would be."
"17541","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr informed us that Mishrah ibn Haan informed him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The people of Yemen are the most tender of hearts and the softest of hearts and the most compliant in obedience."
"17542","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr informed me that Shuayb ibn Zurah informed him, he said: Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying to his companions: Do not frighten yourselves, or he said: souls. So it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, how do we frighten ourselves? He said: Debt."
"17543","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us one day while we were in the Suffah and said: Which of you would love to go early to Buthan or al-Aqiq and bring every day two large-humped bright she-camels and take them without sin or severing kinship? He said: We said: All of us, O Messenger of Allah, would love that. He said: For one of you to go early to the mosque and learn two verses from the Book of Allah is better for him than two camels, and three is better than three, and four is better than four, and according to their number of camels."
"17544","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Mishrah ibn Haan Abu al-Musab al-Maafiri narrated to me, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: If the Quran were in a skin and then thrown into the Fire, it would not burn."
"17545","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Musab narrated to me, he said: I heard Uqbah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Most of the hypocrites of this ummah are its reciters."
"17546","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mishrah ibn Haan narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to say: Indeed most of the hypocrites of this ummah are its reciters."
"17547","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Mishrah ibn Haan, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, was Surah al-Hajj favored over the Quran by placing two prostrations in it? So he said: Yes, and whoever does not prostrate them, let him not recite them."
"17548","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Mishrah ibn Haan narrated to me, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The people embraced Islam and Amr ibn al-Asi believed."
"17549","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Musa, meaning Ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi, narrated to us, my uncle Iyas ibn Amir narrated to me, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: When: So glorify the Name of your Lord the Most Great, was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: Place it in your bowing. Then when: Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High, was revealed, he said: Place it in your prostration."
"17550","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil who said: I did not hear from Uqbah ibn Amir except this hadith."
"17551","Ibn Lahiah said: And Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated it to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The destruction of my ummah is in the Book and milk. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the Book and milk? He said: They learn the Quran and interpret it on other than what Allah, Almighty, revealed, and they love milk, so they leave congregations and Fridays and go to the desert."
"17552","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu al-Khayr saying: I saw Abu Tamim al-Jayshani Abdullah ibn Malik bowing two rakahs when he hears the Maghrib adhan. He said: So I came to Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani and said to him: Shall I not make you wonder at Abu Tamim al-Jayshani bowing two rakahs before the Maghrib prayer, while I want to find fault with him? Uqbah said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I said: What prevents you now? He said: Work."
"17553","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ruayni and Abu Marhum narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi, from Ali ibn Rabah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me to recite the Muawwidhat at the end of every prayer."
"17554","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah and Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, they said: We heard Yazid ibn Abi Habib saying: Abu Imran narrated to me that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I clung to the foot of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me Surah Hud and Surah Yusuf. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Uqbah ibn Amir, you have not recited a surah more beloved to Allah, Almighty, nor more effective with Him than: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak. Yazid said: Abu Imran would not leave it, and he would always recite it in the Maghrib prayer."
"17555","Hajjaj and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no good in one who does not entertain guests."
"17556","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Mishrah ibn Haan al-Maafiri, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: If the Quran were in a skin, the Fire would not touch it."
"17557","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Samh narrated to me, Abu Qabil narrated to me that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed I fear for my ummah two things: the Quran and milk. As for milk, they seek the countryside and follow desires and abandon prayers. And as for the Quran, hypocrites learn it and dispute with it against the believers."
"17558","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Mansur narrated to us, from Dukhayn al-Hajari, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that a group came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he pledged nine and withheld from one. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, you pledged nine and left this one? He said: Upon him is a tamimah. So he put his hand in and cut it, then pledged him, and said: Whoever hangs a tamimah has associated partners."
"17559","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Kab ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A vow is only expiated by the expiation of an oath."
"17560","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya, from Baajah al-Juhani, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided sacrificial animals among his companions, so a jadhaah fell to Uqbah. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, a jadhaah has fallen to me. He said: Sacrifice it."
"17561","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, al-Aslami narrated to me, Abu Ali al-Hamdani narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: We went out with Uqbah ibn Amir on an outing we went on, then a prayer time came, so we asked him to lead us, but he refused us and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: No slave leads people except he bears what was upon them in their prayer; if he does well then for him, and if he does badly then upon him."
"17562","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade cauterization, and he disliked drinking hot water, and when he applied kohl he applied an odd number, and when he cleaned with stones he cleaned with an odd number."
"17563","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr informed me that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you cleans with stones, let him clean with an odd number, and when he applies kohl, let him apply with an odd number."
"17564","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you applies kohl, let him apply with an odd number, and when he cleans with stones, let him clean with an odd number."
"17565","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said, Abu Abd al-Rahman, and I heard it from Harun the same: Ibn Wahb informed me, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Shuayb, he narrated to him that a freedman of Sharhabil ibn Hasanah narrated to him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat whatever your bow returns to you."
"17566","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, that a freedman of Sharhabil ibn Hasanah narrated to him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat whatever your bow returns to you."
"17567","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said, Abdullah, and I think I heard it from him, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr informed me that Hisham ibn Abi Ruqayyah narrated to him, he said: I heard Maslamah ibn Makhlad while sitting on the minbar addressing the people, saying: O people, do you not have in coarse cloth and linen what suffices you from silk? And this man among you informs you from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Stand, O Uqbah. So Uqbah ibn Amir stood, while I was listening, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And I bear witness that I heard him saying: Whoever wears silk in the world will be deprived of wearing it in the Hereafter."
"17568","Harun ibn Maruf and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated it to us, Surayj said: from Amr, Harun said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu Ali Thumamah ibn Shufayy, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying while on the minbar: And prepare for them whatever you can of power. Indeed power is shooting, indeed power is shooting, indeed power is shooting."
"17569","Harun and Surayj ibn Maruf narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu Ali, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Lands will be opened for you and Allah, Almighty, will suffice you, so let none of you be incapable of sporting with his arrows. Surayj said: Thumamah ibn Shufayy."
"17570","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who dies of pleurisy is a martyr."
"17571","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Mishrah ibn Haan narrated to us, that he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever dies guarding in the way of Allah, Almighty, his reward will be continued for him."
"17572","Hasan and Abu Said and Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Mishrah ibn Haan narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Amir, Yahya ibn Ishaq said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Every dead person has his deed sealed except the guard, Yahya said: in the way of Allah, for the reward of his deed will continue for him until Allah, Almighty, resurrects him."
"17573","Ishaq ibn Isa and Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that a boy came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Musa in his hadith: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died and left jewelry, shall I give charity with it on her behalf? He said: Did your mother command you with that? He said: No. He said: Then keep your mother's jewelry."
"17574","Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning al-Muqri, narrated it to us."
"17575","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith and al-Hasan ibn Thawban narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to give charity with jewelry belonging to his mother on behalf of his mother after her death, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Did she command you with that? He said: No. He said: Then no."
"17576","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Ushshanah Hayy ibn Yumin al-Maafiri narrated to us, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The sun draws near to the earth and people sweat. So among people are those whose sweat reaches their heels, and among them those whose reaches half the shin, and among them those whose reaches the knees, and among them those whose reaches the buttocks, and among them those whose reaches the waist, and among them those whose reaches the shoulders, and among them those whose reaches the neck, and among them those whose reaches the middle of the mouth, and he motioned with his hand and bridled his mouth. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, motioning like this. And among them are those whom his sweat covers, and he struck with his hand in gesture."
"17577","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Ushshanah narrated to us, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: When a man purifies himself then comes to the mosque awaiting prayer, his two scribes, or his scribe, write for him for every step he takes to the mosque ten good deeds, and one sitting awaiting prayer is like the devout, and he is recorded among those praying from when he leaves his house until he returns to it."
"17578","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Amr al-Maafiri narrated to us, from one who heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me as a collector, so I asked his permission to eat from the charity, and he permitted me."
"17579","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Ushshanah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Your Lord, Almighty, wonders at a shepherd of sheep on a mountaintop who calls the adhan for prayer and prays, so Allah, Almighty, says: Look at this servant of Mine, he calls the adhan and the iqamah fearing something; I have forgiven him and admitted him to Paradise."
"17580","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Abu Ushshanah al-Maafiri narrated to him, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Your Lord wonders, then he mentioned its meaning, except he said: fearing Me, I have forgiven him and admitted him to Paradise."
"17581","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who recites the Quran aloud is like the one who gives charity aloud, and the one who recites the Quran secretly is like the one who gives charity secretly."
"17582","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Yazid, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying on the minbar: Recite these two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah, for my Lord, Almighty, gave them, or gave them to me, from beneath the Throne."
"17583","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ali ibn Rabah, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed these lineages of yours are not a disgrace upon anyone; all of you are children of Adam, like an unfilled sa measure you have not filled; no one has merit over another except by religion or piety, and it suffices a man to be obscene, miserly, and foul-mouthed."
"17584","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Kab ibn Alqamah, a freedman of Uqbah ibn Amir narrated to me, he said: I said to Uqbah ibn Amir: We have neighbors who drink wine. He said: Conceal for them. He said: I will not conceal for them; I want to go bring the police upon them. He said: Then Uqbah said to him: Woe to you, be gentle with them. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever sees a private fault and conceals it is like one who brought to life a buried girl from her grave."
"17585","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from a man, from Rabiah ibn Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever performs wudu and perfects wudu, then prays neither heedless nor inattentive, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin. And Yahya once said: Forgiven is what was before it of evil deed."
"17586","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to me that a man narrated to him, from Rabiah ibn Qays, that he narrated to him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever performs wudu and perfects wudu, then prays a prayer neither heedless nor inattentive, expiated from him is what was before it."
"17587","Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ruzayq al-Thaqafi, and Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ruzayq al-Thaqafi, from Ibn Shimasah, narrating from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not accept the concession of Allah, Almighty, upon him will be sins like the mountains of Arafah."
"17588","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shimasah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; it is not lawful for a Muslim man to conceal what is in his merchandise from his brother; if he knows of it, he leaves it."
"17589","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Khathami, from Farwah ibn Mujahid al-Lakhmi, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to me: O Uqbah ibn Amir, join whoever cuts you, and give whoever deprives you, and pardon whoever wrongs you."
"17590","He said: Then I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to me: O Uqbah ibn Amir, hold your tongue, and weep over your sin, and let your house suffice you."
"17591","He said: Then I met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to me: O Uqbah ibn Amir, shall I not teach you surahs, the like of which were not revealed in the Torah nor in the Zabur nor in the Gospel nor in the Furqan? No night comes upon you except you recite them in it: Say: He is Allah, One, and say: I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak, and say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. Uqbah said: No night came upon me except I recited them in it, and it is right for me not to leave them, since the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me with them. And Farwah ibn Mujahid, when he narrated this hadith, would say: Indeed how many do not hold the tongue, or do not weep over sin, and the house does not suffice them."
"17592","Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ali ibn Rabah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said of a man called Dhu al-Bijadayn: He is oft-sighing, and that was because he was much in remembrance of Allah, Almighty, in the Quran and raised his voice in supplication."
"17593","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said, Ibn Jurayj said: And Abu Ayyub rode to Uqbah ibn Amir in Egypt and said: I ask you about a matter with none remaining who witnessed it with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except I and you: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, speak about concealing the believer? So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever conceals a believer in the world over a private fault, Allah, Almighty, will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection. Then he returned to Medina, not even unpacking his mount, narrating this hadith."
"17594","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu Imran, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he said: I followed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was riding, so I placed my hand on his foot and said: Teach me Surah Hud or Surah Yusuf. So he said: You will never recite anything more effective with Allah than: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak."
"17595","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from a shaykh from Maafir, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When a man performs wudu then comes to the mosque, Allah, Almighty, writes for him for every step he takes ten good deeds. Then if he prays in the mosque and sits in it, he is like the fasting devout until he returns."
"17596","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Ushshanah narrated to us, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I do not say today upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what he did not say. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever says upon me what I did not say, let him take a house in Hell."
"17597","And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Two men from my ummah, one of them rises by night and forces himself to purification while knots are upon him. So he performs wudu, and when he washes his hands a knot loosens, and when he wipes his head a knot loosens, and when he washes his face a knot loosens, and when he wipes his head a knot loosens, and when he washes his feet a knot loosens. Then the Lord, Almighty, says to those behind the veil: Look at this servant of Mine forcing himself; whatever this servant of Mine asks Me, it is his."
"17598","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Qabil narrated to us, from Abu Ushshanah al-Maafiri, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever leaves his house to the mosque, written for him for every step he takes is ten good deeds, and one sitting in the mosque awaiting prayer is like the devout, and he is recorded among those praying until he returns to his house."
"17599","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever leaves his house, then he mentioned like it."
"17600","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, from Ibn Lahiah, Abu Qabil narrated to me, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever leaves his house, then he mentioned the hadith."
